                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "ac54acc9-4397-3ed1-bd63-c1645550ebc7",
                        "entry_id": "959a5c05-09bf-300d-85c0-07c5ba4d5f90",
                        "glosses": [
                            "название ряда промысловых рыб из рода Корюшки (лат. Osmerus) и Малоротые корюшки (лат. Hypomesus)"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c34cd083-09a8-433b-90eb-d2e11ca652ad",
                                "sense_id": "ac54acc9-4397-3ed1-bd63-c1645550ebc7",
                                "text": "Жарили корюшку так: разрезали ножницами брюхо, внутренности выбрасывали, а рыбу жарили с головой. Андрюша, приятно удивленный нежным вкусом неприглядной рыбки, предложил зажарить ее целиком, как есть, — зачем же добру пропадать, заметил с интернатской смекалкой; этот метод через неделю опробовали на компании приехавших из Москвы Жукиных испанцев, и потом уже корюшку в семье готовили именно так — обваливая в муке, жарили вместе с потрохами, и так аппетитно хрустели солоноватые ломкие плавники и хвостики!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "e9a579cf-a481-4359-a5f3-66574edaba4a",
                        "source_entry_id": "959a5c05-09bf-300d-85c0-07c5ba4d5f90",
                        "source_sense_id": "ac54acc9-4397-3ed1-bd63-c1645550ebc7",
                        "target_lang_word": "smelt",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "smelt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "c95cae1b-619f-330b-bd11-6a086d18b89e",
                                        "entry_id": "db58e3ab-dcee-385a-b2ea-04cc51d930d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any small anadromous fish of the family Osmeridae, found in the Atlantic and Pacific Oceans and in lakes in North America and northern part of Europe."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "80dc824e-71c1-344e-9d99-b72baf4aeecc",
                                        "entry_id": "db58e3ab-dcee-385a-b2ea-04cc51d930d6",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A fool; a simpleton."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bbfd6429-523d-42a8-9747-c1e3c1a65c21",
                                                "sense_id": "80dc824e-71c1-344e-9d99-b72baf4aeecc",
                                                "text": "These direct Men, they are no Men of fashion, Talk what you will , this is a very Smelt"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "smelt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "78b108ff-d841-3f2c-8b01-c4e81cfb690a",
                                        "entry_id": "639f9e7f-8806-3d00-b7e7-e6129d8fc84d",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "simple past and past participle of smell"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "form-of",
                                            "participle",
                                            "past"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "smelt",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f823d2ea-0b0c-3191-bea7-cd60f3463524",
                                        "entry_id": "d32a4705-9701-349e-985d-491ff5fdaca7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Production of metal, especially iron, from ore in a process that involves heating and chemical reduction of metal compounds into purified metal."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "2797e17a-5c14-3aa8-ae88-46671811e56e",
                                        "entry_id": "d32a4705-9701-349e-985d-491ff5fdaca7",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Any of the various liquids or semi-molten solids produced and used during the course of such production."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "116ee6b3-e4b9-4875-ac06-a3e296da516f",
                                                "sense_id": "2797e17a-5c14-3aa8-ae88-46671811e56e",
                                                "text": "1982, Raymond E. Kirk and Donald F. Othmer, Encyclopedia of Chemical Technology, Wiley, →ISBN, page 405,\nThe green liquor, ie, [sic] the solution obtained on dissolving the smelt, contains an insoluble residue called dregs, which gives it a dark green appearance."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "999a4521-3e01-4ee5-9ac4-dd504acd57ad",
                                                "sense_id": "2797e17a-5c14-3aa8-ae88-46671811e56e",
                                                "text": "1996, Arthur J. Wilson, The Living Rock: The Story of Metals Since Earliest Time and Their Impact on Civilization,\nWhen the smelt was complete the crucible could be lifted out and the metal poured directly into the moulds, thus avoiding the need to break it up and remelt […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b6a395dd-885d-4f5e-9042-1c637658aa92",
                                                "sense_id": "2797e17a-5c14-3aa8-ae88-46671811e56e",
                                                "text": "2000, Julian Henderson, The Science and Archaeology of Materials: An Investigation of Inorganic Materials,\n[…] can vary in different positions in the furnace and during the smelt.\nFurnaces are unlikely to survive the smelts; all that often remains on metal production sites is just furnace bases and broken fragments of furnaces […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8b6c70c4-6a4d-4dbc-8631-84953c3575d8",
                                                "sense_id": "2797e17a-5c14-3aa8-ae88-46671811e56e",
                                                "text": "2002, Jenny Moore, “Who Lights the Fire? Gender and the Energy of Production”, in Moira Donald and Linda Hurcombe (eds.), Gender and Material Culture in Archaeological Perspective, Palgrave Macmillan, →ISBN, page 130,\nWomen are allowed to play some small part in the smelt if they are breastfeeding or post-menopausal (van der Merwe and Avery, 1988)."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
